; Stage 15 W9 defect 21: a SECOND namespace declaring a protocol with the same
; bare name `Describe` as lib/nsdescribe.nuc's, and a different required method.
;
; This is the point of the ruling that protocols are namespaced: `dp/Describe`
; and `dp2/Describe` are two protocols, one type may conform to both, and a
; `(dyn dp/Describe)` box must dispatch `describe` while a `(dyn dp2/Describe)`
; box of the same type dispatches `tag-of`. Under the pre-W9 bare keying the two
; would have been one protocol and the second `defprotocol` a silent no-op.
;
; The required method is deliberately NOT named `describe`: two namespaces
; defining a same-named *function* collapse into one generic mangled under the
; first-seen namespace's ir-prefix, which is an unrelated (and still open)
; function-namespacing gap. Keeping the method names distinct isolates this test
; to protocol identity.

(ns dp2)

(defprotocol Describe (tag-of ((self (ref Self))) i32))
